  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🔦 Ghost Hunting Team Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for paranormal investigation groups, from serious research societies to the Cold Spot Collective."
    },
    "intro": "A good ghost hunting team name sounds either serious enough to be trusted with an old house at midnight, or honest about the fact that you'll scream at a creaking floorboard. Every group of torch-carrying, flask-packing investigators needs a name for the T-shirts. This **ghost hunting team name generator** makes names for paranormal teams and ghost hunting groups: serious research societies, spooky night watches, funny crews and teams named after a town or moor.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good ghost hunting team names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Wessex Paranormal Investigations</strong>: a serious name with an old regional title.</li><li><strong>The Ellery Bureau of Apparition Studies</strong>: sounds like it has a filing cabinet full of cases.</li><li><strong>Residual Energy Monitoring Group</strong>: borrows the language of ghost hunters' kit.</li><li><strong>The Hushed Guard</strong>: spooky and short, good on a hoodie.</li><li><strong>Last Light Callers</strong>: a team that starts when everyone else goes home.</li><li><strong>The Faintly Terrified Crew</strong>: honest about how the night will go.</li><li><strong>Phantoms Anonymous</strong>: a joke that works on a podcast or a T-shirt.</li><li><strong>The Llandeilo Spectral Society</strong>: a local group named after its town.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How ghost hunting groups name themselves",
